# 01 - Jenkins Freestyle CI

## Real-World Scenario

A development team maintains application source code in GitHub.
The DevOps team needs Jenkins to retrieve the latest source code
from the repository and verify that Jenkins can successfully
connect to GitHub and check out the required branch.

## Objective

Build the first Jenkins CI workflow using a Freestyle project.

The workflow should:

1. Connect Jenkins to GitHub using SSH.
2. Retrieve the source code from the `main` branch.
3. Check out the latest Git revision.
4. Store the source code in the Jenkins workspace.
5. Complete the Jenkins build successfully.

